cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these measurements, please cite this repository."
title: "Decentralized AI: cross-device LLM inference benchmark on a PC and an Android phone"
abstract: >-
  Measured layer-pipelined LLM inference across a Windows laptop and an Android phone
  using llama.cpp RPC. Single machine 24.98 tok/s, loopback RPC 20.28 tok/s (-19%),
  PC + phone over 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi 3.40 tok/s (-83%). The 19% is architecture tax; the 83%
  is network tax. Concludes that layer splitting adds capacity, not speed, and that MoE
  is the only form where pooling wins on both.
